WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.664
Fixed verbs. Past and order.

2
00:00:03.014 --> 00:00:04.903
Two kinds of verb that never change.

3
00:00:05.153 --> 00:00:07.820
A past verb and an order
verb are always fixed.

4
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.978
Their ending tells you who did the action.

5
00:00:10.078 --> 00:00:12.157
And that ending never moves for iʿrāb.

6
00:00:12.707 --> 00:00:14.600
Chapter one. Which verbs are fixed?

7
00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.564
Arabic has three kinds of verb.

8
00:00:16.664 --> 00:00:18.718
Two of them are fixed in every form.

9
00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:19.919
‫مَبْنِيٌّ‬

10
00:00:20.369 --> 00:00:23.416
The first is the past verb.
An action that is done.

11
00:00:23.666 --> 00:00:24.407
‫كَتَبَ‬

12
00:00:24.707 --> 00:00:26.204
He wrote. It is fixed.

13
00:00:26.454 --> 00:00:29.528
The second is the order verb.
You tell someone to act.

14
00:00:29.778 --> 00:00:30.595
‫اُكْتُبْ‬

15
00:00:30.895 --> 00:00:32.512
Write! It is fixed too.

16
00:00:32.762 --> 00:00:37.319
The third is the present verb. It is
mostly flexible. Its ending changes.

17
00:00:37.419 --> 00:00:38.883
We study it in Stage 8.

18
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:41.948
In this unit we only use
past and order verbs.

19
00:00:42.048 --> 00:00:43.803
Leave the present verb for later.

20
00:00:46.067 --> 00:00:49.214
Chapter two. The past
verb. Fourteen persons.

21
00:00:49.464 --> 00:00:51.006
Learn this table by heart.

22
00:00:51.106 --> 00:00:53.870
Each pronoun from unit
one has its own past form.

23
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:57.439
Start with he, they two,
and they. These are for men.

24
00:00:57.689 --> 00:00:58.430
‫كَتَبَ‬

25
00:00:58.680 --> 00:00:59.524
‫كَتَبَا‬

26
00:00:59.774 --> 00:01:00.748
‫كَتَبُوا‬

27
00:01:01.098 --> 00:01:03.104
Now she, they two, and they, for women.

28
00:01:03.354 --> 00:01:04.270
‫كَتَبَتْ‬

29
00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:05.475
‫كَتَبَتَا‬

30
00:01:05.725 --> 00:01:06.648
‫كَتَبْنَ‬

31
00:01:06.998 --> 00:01:09.686
Now you. One man, two men, and many men.

32
00:01:09.936 --> 00:01:10.786
‫كَتَبْتَ‬

33
00:01:11.036 --> 00:01:12.128
‫كَتَبْتُمَا‬

34
00:01:12.378 --> 00:01:13.424
‫كَتَبْتُمْ‬

35
00:01:13.774 --> 00:01:16.928
You again. One woman, two
women, and many women.

36
00:01:17.178 --> 00:01:18.088
‫كَتَبْتِ‬

37
00:01:18.338 --> 00:01:19.430
‫كَتَبْتُمَا‬

38
00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.001
‫كَتَبْتُنَّ‬

39
00:01:21.351 --> 00:01:22.387
Last, I and we.

40
00:01:22.637 --> 00:01:23.540
‫كَتَبْتُ‬

41
00:01:23.790 --> 00:01:24.729
‫كَتَبْنَا‬

42
00:01:25.079 --> 00:01:26.388
That is the whole table.

43
00:01:26.838 --> 00:01:30.073
There are fourteen persons, but
only thirteen written forms.

44
00:01:30.173 --> 00:01:31.265
‫كَتَبْتُمَا‬

45
00:01:31.565 --> 00:01:34.697
You two wrote. It is used for
two men and for two women.

46
00:01:35.147 --> 00:01:36.116
Three examples.

47
00:01:36.266 --> 00:01:37.440
I went to the mosque.

48
00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:41.032
‫أَنَا ذَهَبْتُ إِلَى المَسْجِدِ‬

49
00:01:41.382 --> 00:01:42.995
The verb has the ending for I.

50
00:01:43.345 --> 00:01:44.620
She sat in the room.

51
00:01:44.870 --> 00:01:47.346
‫هِيَ جَلَسَتْ فِي الغُرْفَةِ‬

52
00:01:47.696 --> 00:01:49.295
The verb has the form for she.

53
00:01:49.645 --> 00:01:51.226
We did not go out of the house.

54
00:01:51.476 --> 00:01:54.564
‫نَحْنُ مَا خَرَجْنَا مِنَ البَيْتِ‬

55
00:01:54.914 --> 00:01:57.004
Look at the small word before the verb.

56
00:01:57.254 --> 00:01:57.969
‫مَا‬

57
00:01:58.269 --> 00:02:02.564
Before a past verb, it means did not.
We come back to it in chapter five.

58
00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.981
Chapter three. The ending is the doer.

59
00:02:07.231 --> 00:02:10.167
Most endings of the past
verb are attached pronouns.

60
00:02:10.267 --> 00:02:13.713
The pronoun is the doer. It is
fixed, in the place of rafʿ.

61
00:02:13.963 --> 00:02:16.303
‫فِي مَحَلِّ رَفْعٍ‬

62
00:02:16.753 --> 00:02:18.235
Here are the doer endings.

63
00:02:18.385 --> 00:02:19.744
This ending means I.

64
00:02:19.894 --> 00:02:20.880
You, for one man.

65
00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:22.199
You, for one woman.

66
00:02:22.349 --> 00:02:23.097
And we.

67
00:02:23.247 --> 00:02:24.268
You all, for men.

68
00:02:24.418 --> 00:02:25.333
They, for men.

69
00:02:25.483 --> 00:02:26.421
They, for women.

70
00:02:26.571 --> 00:02:27.481
And they two.

71
00:02:27.731 --> 00:02:29.523
Each of these endings is the doer.

72
00:02:29.973 --> 00:02:31.490
But one ending is different.

73
00:02:31.740 --> 00:02:32.656
‫كَتَبَتْ‬

74
00:02:32.956 --> 00:02:36.504
She wrote. Here the ending only
shows that the doer is feminine.

75
00:02:36.604 --> 00:02:38.173
It is a ḥarf, with no place.

76
00:02:38.273 --> 00:02:40.282
The doer is hidden. It is she.

77
00:02:40.532 --> 00:02:41.213
‫هِيَ‬

78
00:02:41.663 --> 00:02:43.157
So compare three forms.

79
00:02:43.307 --> 00:02:44.608
First, a hidden doer.

80
00:02:44.758 --> 00:02:45.499
‫كَتَبَ‬

81
00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:48.934
There is no ending. The
doer is hidden. It is he.

82
00:02:49.284 --> 00:02:50.859
Second, a hidden doer again.

83
00:02:51.009 --> 00:02:51.925
‫كَتَبَتْ‬

84
00:02:52.225 --> 00:02:55.515
This ending is a ḥarf. The
doer is hidden. It is she.

85
00:02:55.865 --> 00:02:57.342
Third, an attached doer.

86
00:02:57.492 --> 00:02:58.395
‫كَتَبْتُ‬

87
00:02:58.695 --> 00:03:00.868
The ending is the doer,
in the place of rafʿ.

88
00:03:01.318 --> 00:03:04.060
When a noun is the doer,
the verb has no doer ending.

89
00:03:04.310 --> 00:03:06.094
‫كَتَبَ الطَّالِبُ‬

90
00:03:06.444 --> 00:03:08.874
The student wrote. The
student is the doer.

91
00:03:09.424 --> 00:03:12.195
Chapter four. What the
past verb is built on.

92
00:03:12.445 --> 00:03:15.096
A fixed word is built on one fixed mark.

93
00:03:15.096 --> 00:03:18.145
A past verb is built on
fatha, damma or sukūn.

94
00:03:18.245 --> 00:03:22.145
Look at the last letter of the verb
itself, before any doer pronoun.

95
00:03:22.495 --> 00:03:25.281
The past verb is built on
fatha when it has no ending.

96
00:03:25.381 --> 00:03:30.052
It is also built on fatha before the ḥarf
for she, and before the alif for they two.

97
00:03:30.302 --> 00:03:31.043
‫كَتَبَ‬

98
00:03:31.243 --> 00:03:32.159
‫كَتَبَتْ‬

99
00:03:32.359 --> 00:03:33.203
‫كَتَبَا‬

100
00:03:33.403 --> 00:03:34.358
‫كَتَبَتَا‬

101
00:03:34.708 --> 00:03:37.845
It is built on damma before
the ending for they, for men.

102
00:03:38.095 --> 00:03:39.069
‫كَتَبُوا‬

103
00:03:39.419 --> 00:03:42.191
It is built on sukūn before
all the other endings.

104
00:03:42.441 --> 00:03:43.344
‫كَتَبْتُ‬

105
00:03:43.544 --> 00:03:44.483
‫كَتَبْنَا‬

106
00:03:44.683 --> 00:03:45.606
‫كَتَبْنَ‬

107
00:03:45.956 --> 00:03:49.254
Before these endings, the last
letter of the verb has sukūn.

108
00:03:49.704 --> 00:03:51.165
One more look at she wrote.

109
00:03:51.415 --> 00:03:52.331
‫كَتَبَتْ‬

110
00:03:52.631 --> 00:03:56.489
It is built on fatha. The fatha is
on the letter before the ending.

111
00:03:56.589 --> 00:03:58.598
The sukūn sits on the ḥarf after it.

112
00:03:58.698 --> 00:04:02.597
That sukūn belongs to the ḥarf.
The verb itself is built on fatha.

113
00:04:04.833 --> 00:04:06.568
Chapter five. Saying did not.

114
00:04:06.818 --> 00:04:10.078
To say did not, put this word
right before the past verb.

115
00:04:10.328 --> 00:04:11.043
‫مَا‬

116
00:04:11.343 --> 00:04:14.554
The verb does not change at
all. Same form, same doer.

117
00:04:15.004 --> 00:04:15.944
He did not write.

118
00:04:16.094 --> 00:04:17.222
‫مَا كَتَبَ‬

119
00:04:17.522 --> 00:04:18.582
She did not write.

120
00:04:18.732 --> 00:04:20.007
‫مَا كَتَبَتْ‬

121
00:04:20.307 --> 00:04:21.265
I did not go.

122
00:04:21.415 --> 00:04:22.834
‫مَا ذَهَبْتُ‬

123
00:04:23.134 --> 00:04:24.258
They did not go out.

124
00:04:24.408 --> 00:04:25.676
‫مَا خَرَجُوا‬

125
00:04:26.126 --> 00:04:28.187
This word means not. It is a ḥarf.

126
00:04:28.287 --> 00:04:29.884
It is fixed, with no place.

127
00:04:30.134 --> 00:04:33.562
‫لَا مَحَلَّ لَهُ مِنَ الإِعْرَابِ‬

128
00:04:33.912 --> 00:04:35.935
It does not change the verb after it.

129
00:04:36.485 --> 00:04:37.962
I did not go to the market.

130
00:04:38.212 --> 00:04:41.143
‫مَا ذَهَبْتُ إِلَى السُّوقِ‬

131
00:04:41.493 --> 00:04:44.460
The ending for I is still the
doer, in the place of rafʿ.

132
00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:47.062
The student did not go
out of the classroom.

133
00:04:47.312 --> 00:04:50.632
‫مَا خَرَجَ الطَّالِبُ مِنَ الفَصْلِ‬

134
00:04:51.082 --> 00:04:52.426
We did not open the door.

135
00:04:52.676 --> 00:04:54.679
‫مَا فَتَحْنَا البَابَ‬

136
00:04:55.129 --> 00:04:58.154
Did you write the lesson?
No, I did not write it.

137
00:04:58.404 --> 00:05:02.000
‫هَلْ كَتَبْتَ الدَّرْسَ؟‬
‫لَا، مَا كَتَبْتُهُ‬

138
00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.826
In the answer, the first
small word means no.

139
00:05:04.976 --> 00:05:05.715
‫لَا‬

140
00:05:05.965 --> 00:05:07.957
The second one makes the verb did not.

141
00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:08.822
‫مَا‬

142
00:05:09.372 --> 00:05:11.743
Do not mix up two words
that look the same.

143
00:05:11.843 --> 00:05:14.260
The word for did not is
a ḥarf, with no place.

144
00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:18.460
The one in unit five means what.
It is an ism, and it has a place.

145
00:05:18.710 --> 00:05:19.719
‫مَا هَذَا؟‬

146
00:05:20.019 --> 00:05:20.945
What is this?

147
00:05:21.395 --> 00:05:23.052
You already know the word for no.

148
00:05:23.302 --> 00:05:24.041
‫لَا‬

149
00:05:24.341 --> 00:05:28.826
With the present verb, it also means
do not. That comes later in the course.

150
00:05:28.926 --> 00:05:30.987
With the past verb, we use the other word.

151
00:05:31.237 --> 00:05:31.952
‫مَا‬

152
00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:36.916
Chapter six. The order verb. Five forms.

153
00:05:37.166 --> 00:05:39.541
You give an order to the
person in front of you.

154
00:05:39.641 --> 00:05:41.206
So there are only five forms.

155
00:05:41.556 --> 00:05:42.502
To you, a man.

156
00:05:42.652 --> 00:05:43.469
‫اُكْتُبْ‬

157
00:05:43.769 --> 00:05:46.902
Built on sukūn. The doer
is hidden. It is you.

158
00:05:47.052 --> 00:05:47.881
‫أَنْتَ‬

159
00:05:48.231 --> 00:05:49.218
To you, a woman.

160
00:05:49.368 --> 00:05:50.442
‫اُكْتُبِي‬

161
00:05:50.742 --> 00:05:53.561
Built on dropping the noon.
The ending is the doer.

162
00:05:53.911 --> 00:05:54.854
To you two.

163
00:05:55.004 --> 00:05:56.038
‫اُكْتُبَا‬

164
00:05:56.338 --> 00:05:58.653
The same here. Built on dropping the noon.

165
00:05:59.003 --> 00:05:59.907
To you, men.

166
00:06:00.057 --> 00:06:01.122
‫اُكْتُبُوا‬

167
00:06:01.422 --> 00:06:04.538
And again, dropping the
noon. The ending is the doer.

168
00:06:04.888 --> 00:06:05.783
To you, women.

169
00:06:05.933 --> 00:06:06.992
‫اُكْتُبْنَ‬

170
00:06:07.292 --> 00:06:09.542
Built on sukūn. The ending is the doer.

171
00:06:09.992 --> 00:06:11.639
So there are two ways to be built.

172
00:06:11.789 --> 00:06:13.482
Two forms are built on sukūn.

173
00:06:13.632 --> 00:06:15.781
Three forms are built
on dropping the noon.

174
00:06:15.931 --> 00:06:18.758
You will see where that
noon comes from in Stage 8.

175
00:06:19.308 --> 00:06:20.423
Sit down, Aminah.

176
00:06:20.673 --> 00:06:23.078
‫اِجْلِسِي يَا آمِنَةُ‬

177
00:06:23.428 --> 00:06:24.971
The order is to one woman.

178
00:06:25.321 --> 00:06:28.479
Go out of the classroom.
This is to a group of men.

179
00:06:28.729 --> 00:06:31.218
‫اُخْرُجُوا مِنَ الفَصْلِ‬

180
00:06:31.768 --> 00:06:36.208
Chapter seven. Alif with damma, or
alif with kasra? A list to learn.

181
00:06:36.458 --> 00:06:38.457
The order verb starts with a helping alif.

182
00:06:38.557 --> 00:06:40.718
Look at the middle
letter of the order verb.

183
00:06:40.818 --> 00:06:45.460
If it has damma, start with alif and
damma. If not, start with alif and kasra.

184
00:06:45.810 --> 00:06:48.175
In the first four, the
middle letter has damma.

185
00:06:48.425 --> 00:06:49.242
‫اُكْتُبْ‬

186
00:06:49.492 --> 00:06:50.446
‫اُدْرُسْ‬

187
00:06:50.696 --> 00:06:51.620
‫اُخْرُجْ‬

188
00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:52.805
‫اُدْخُلْ‬

189
00:06:53.105 --> 00:06:54.853
So they start with alif and damma.

190
00:06:55.203 --> 00:06:59.091
In the next four, the middle letter
has fatha or kasra. No damma.

191
00:06:59.341 --> 00:07:00.245
‫اِذْهَبْ‬

192
00:07:00.495 --> 00:07:01.427
‫اِجْلِسْ‬

193
00:07:01.677 --> 00:07:02.579
‫اِفْتَحْ‬

194
00:07:02.829 --> 00:07:03.696
‫اِشْرَبْ‬

195
00:07:03.996 --> 00:07:05.906
So they start with alif and kasra.

196
00:07:06.356 --> 00:07:09.889
The past verb does not tell you
the middle vowel of the order verb.

197
00:07:09.989 --> 00:07:11.991
So learn each order verb as a word.

198
00:07:14.233 --> 00:07:17.192
Chapter eight. The helping
kasra, from Stage 2.

199
00:07:17.442 --> 00:07:19.899
A word cannot end in
sukūn right before al.

200
00:07:19.999 --> 00:07:23.888
So the sukūn becomes a small
kasra. The verb is still fixed.

201
00:07:24.238 --> 00:07:25.166
Open the door.

202
00:07:25.416 --> 00:07:27.099
‫اِفْتَحِ البَابَ‬

203
00:07:27.449 --> 00:07:31.650
The order verb ends in sukūn.
Before al, it takes a small kasra.

204
00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:33.340
It is still built on sukūn.

205
00:07:33.690 --> 00:07:35.429
The girl did not write the lesson.

206
00:07:35.679 --> 00:07:38.520
‫مَا كَتَبَتِ البِنْتُ الدَّرْسَ‬

207
00:07:38.870 --> 00:07:41.575
Here the kasra sits on the
ḥarf at the end of the verb.

208
00:07:41.675 --> 00:07:43.506
And the word for not changes nothing.

209
00:07:43.856 --> 00:07:48.638
This kasra is only a bridge for
speaking. It is not jarr, and not iʿrāb.

210
00:07:49.288 --> 00:07:50.140
In short.

211
00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:54.878
Past and order verbs are fixed. The
present verb is mostly flexible.

212
00:07:54.878 --> 00:07:56.228
It comes in Stage 8.

213
00:07:56.378 --> 00:07:58.241
The past verb has fourteen persons.

214
00:07:58.391 --> 00:08:01.759
Endings like these are doer
pronouns, in the place of rafʿ.

215
00:08:01.759 --> 00:08:03.928
But the ending of she wrote is a ḥarf.

216
00:08:04.078 --> 00:08:07.368
The past verb is built on
fatha, on damma, or on sukūn.

217
00:08:07.518 --> 00:08:10.261
To say did not, put this
word before a past verb.

218
00:08:10.411 --> 00:08:11.539
‫مَا كَتَبَ‬

219
00:08:11.789 --> 00:08:13.393
It is a ḥarf with no place.

220
00:08:13.543 --> 00:08:16.754
The order verb is built on
sukūn, or on dropping the noon.

221
00:08:16.904 --> 00:08:21.025
A middle damma gives alif with
damma. Otherwise, alif with kasra.

222
00:08:21.475 --> 00:08:24.109
Now it is your turn.
Open the Practice tab.

223
00:08:24.259 --> 00:08:27.924
Choose the past form, say what it
is built on, and give the order.

224
00:08:28.074 --> 00:08:28.806
Good luck.
